      ":question/id": "4eff42d8-d1d0-524c-93c8-09ae369be166",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-24145",
      ":question/problem": "A forex trader realizes that her annual profits have been growing continuously at a rate of $15 \\mathrm{\\% }$ per year. If she currently has a profit of $\\$16700$ this year, what was her profit $5$ years ago? Round your answer to the nearest dollar.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. Here $P=16700$, $r=0.15$ per year, and $t=5$ years. Solve for the earlier profit $P_0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n16700 &= P_0e^{(0.15)(5)} \\\\\nP_0 &= \\frac{16700}{e^{0.75}} \\\\\n&\\approx 7888.5214.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest dollar, the profit five years ago was $\\$7889$."
    },
