      ":question/id": "156b3546-d17b-59f0-814e-f2278503aff8",
      ":question/problem": "A forex trader's annual profits have been *decreasing* continuously at a rate of $9\\%$ per year. Her profit this year is $\\$18300$. What was her profit $2$ years ago? Round your answer to the nearest dollar.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the continuously compounded growth equation $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The current amount is $P=18300$, the rate is $r=-0.09$ (negative for decay), and the elapsed time is $t=2$ years. The time unit matches the rate. Substitute and divide by the exponential factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n18300 &= P_0e^{(-0.09)(2)} \\\\\n18300 &= P_0e^{-0.18} \\\\\ne^{-0.18} &\\approx 0.83527021 \\\\\nP_0 &= \\frac{18300}{e^{-0.18}} \\\\\n&\\approx 21909\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe earlier profit was $\\$21909$. Round only the final amount; keep full calculator precision in the exponential factor."
    },
