      ":question/id": "28a7be87-9d22-5ff4-8dc9-8b5b93aae8ae",
      ":question/problem": "A forex trader's annual profits have been *decreasing* continuously at a rate of $13\\%$ per year. Her profit this year is $\\$36550$. What was her profit $7$ years ago? Round your answer to the nearest dollar.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the continuously compounded growth equation $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The current amount is $P=36550$, the rate is $r=-0.13$ (negative for decay), and the elapsed time is $t=7$ years. The time unit matches the rate. Substitute and divide by the exponential factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n36550 &= P_0e^{(-0.13)(7)} \\\\\n36550 &= P_0e^{-0.91} \\\\\ne^{-0.91} &\\approx 0.40252422 \\\\\nP_0 &= \\frac{36550}{e^{-0.91}} \\\\\n&\\approx 90802\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe earlier profit was $\\$90802$. Round only the final amount; keep full calculator precision in the exponential factor."
